  -- Caldwell Jackson (YEA) -> Transportation
  ('92bb2ff8-0967-41c3-a68a-efc7a072ead1','ba59337e-30e2-4aba-a39a-426b3366eb27',$r$Voted Yea on LD 427, "An Act to Prohibit Mandatory Parking Space Minimums in State and Municipal Building Codes" (Maine House Roll Call #534, 6/16/2025; passed 82-65 and signed as Public Law Chapter 374), which bars state and municipal building codes from imposing mandatory parking-space minimums. On this ladder "reduce parking requirements communitywide" appears in stance 1 and in no other stance, and the bill is a statewide repeal of exactly that mandate, so the vote is evidence for stance 1 rather than merely a direction. Honest limit, stated so it can be argued with: this is a single roll call. It does not by itself evidence the pedestrian, cycling and transit investment that stance 1 also describes, and no other transportation instrument for this member was examined. This row was re-filed from Residential Zoning, where the same vote had been graded against the wrong ladder.$r$,ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280096272&chamber=H&serialnumber=534','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=427']::text[]),
